    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it's green. The build succeeds with **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and consolidated duplicate detection onto it, per the spec.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.identityKey`** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 now returns the SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` instead of the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`. This makes the DTO's `identityKey` a 64-char lowercase hex string and removes `householdId` from the key.\n\n**`OwnerRegistrar`** (`rest/controller/OwnerRegistrar.java`):\n- `isDuplicateOwner` still keys on `identityKey` (409), still filters out `deleted` owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first \u2014 unchanged in structure, but now over the new key.\n- `possibleDuplicateOf` (soft-match) now triggers when the **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName)** and **postcode** both match, replacing the old exact-lastName + different-telephone rule.\n- Removed the `householdMember` guard that previously suppressed soft-matches for same-household owners, so two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are now created as a soft match rather than being a hard household duplicate. `householdId` is still computed and used for the membership-level ceiling / household-size derivations.\n\n**`HouseholdResolver`** \u2014 removed the now-dead `householdExists` method (the retired household-duplicate 409 path) and its unused `ClinicService` dependency, and updated the javadoc to note the id no longer drives duplicate detection.\n\nThe soft-match \"identityKey differs\" check is effectively guaranteed at that point (any exact-key match would already have been rejected as a 409), but I kept it explicit to mirror the spec wording exactly.",
